<article class="env-definition" id="0CMR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CMR">Definition <span data-tag="0CMR">102.3.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a $1$-morphism of categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. We say $f$ is <em>limit preserving</em> if for every directed limit $U = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits U_ i$ of affine schemes over $S$ the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathcal{X}_{U_ i} \ar[r] \ar[d]_ f &  \mathcal{X}_ U \ar[d]^ f \\  \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathcal{Y}_{U_ i} \ar[r] &  \mathcal{Y}_ U }  \]
</div>
  <p> of fibre categories is $2$-cartesian. </p>
</article>